 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "The most famous bluff in Chinese history was a wide-open gate.",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 2.538
  },
  {
   "text": "It's the year two twenty-eight,",
   "s": 3.349,
   "e": 4.269
  },
  {
   "text": "and China is split into three kingdoms at war.",
   "s": 4.557,
   "e": 6.528
  },
  {
   "text": "Zhuge Liang,",
   "s": 7.354,
   "e": 7.94
  },
  {
   "text": "the genius strategist of Shu,",
   "s": 8.222,
   "e": 9.547
  },
  {
   "text": "has a terrible problem.",
   "s": 9.774,
   "e": 10.6
  },
  {
   "text": "His general Ma Su ignored orders and lost a mountain pass.",
   "s": 11.381,
   "e": 14.049
  },
  {
   "text": "Now, the story goes,",
   "s": 14.467,
   "e": 15.383
  },
  {
   "text": "a hundred and fifty thousand enemy soldiers are marching on the tiny town of Xicheng.",
   "s": 15.771,
   "e": 18.94
  },
  {
   "text": "Leading them is his greatest rival,",
   "s": 19.505,
   "e": 20.755
  },
  {
   "text": "Sima Yi.",
   "s": 20.962,
   "e": 21.567
  },
  {
   "text": "And inside the walls?",
   "s": 22.354,
   "e": 23.176
  },
  {
   "text": "A few thousand men.",
   "s": 24.04,
   "e": 24.757
  },
  {
   "text": "Mostly cooks, clerks,",
   "s": 25.328,
   "e": 25.978
  },
  {
   "text": "and very nervous horses.",
   "s": 26.244,
   "e": 27.443
  },
  {
   "text": "He can't fight.",
   "s": 28.134,
   "e": 28.62
  },
  {
   "text": "He can't run.",
   "s": 29.178,
   "e": 29.626
  },
  {
   "text": "So he does the strangest thing imaginable.",
   "s": 30.455,
   "e": 32.015
  },
  {
   "text": "He throws the gates open.",
   "s": 32.886,
   "e": 33.708
  },
  {
   "text": "Soldiers dressed as townsfolk sweep the road.",
   "s": 34.247,
   "e": 35.961
  },
  {
   "text": "And Zhuge Liang sits on top of the wall and plays the zither.",
   "s": 36.549,
   "e": 38.851
  },
  {
   "text": "Sima Yi rides up and stares.",
   "s": 39.606,
   "e": 41.059
  },
  {
   "text": "Zhuge Liang never takes risks.",
   "s": 41.876,
   "e": 43.287
  },
  {
   "text": "An open gate means a trap.",
   "s": 43.783,
   "e": 44.847
  },
  {
   "text": "It has to be.",
   "s": 45.725,
   "e": 46.285
  },
  {
   "text": "So he turns his army around and leaves.",
   "s": 47.161,
   "e": 48.701
  },
  {
   "text": "One man and a song beat a hundred and fifty thousand.",
   "s": 49.365,
   "e": 51.492
  },
  {
   "text": "Sometimes the best defense is letting your enemy scare himself.",
   "s": 52.245,
   "e": 54.526
  }
 ]
